  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nA weak low pressure system off the California coast on Saturday\nwill move slowly inland into California on Sunday and Monday with\nnot much change in high temperatures on Sunday. Monday high\ntemperatures will cool a few to around 5 degrees. High pressure to\nthe east will bring warming for Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nHigh temperatures on Monday will be as much as 4 to 8 degrees \nbelow average for the valleys into the mountains with high \ntemperatures on Monday ranging from the lower to mid 70s near the\ncoast to the lower to mid 80s for the Inland Empire with the upper\n90s for the lower deserts. \n\nHigh temperatures on Wednesday will warm to within a few degrees\nof average with the high temperatures ranging from the mid to \nupper 70s near the coast to the upper 80s to mid 90s for the \nInland Empire with the lower deserts around 100.",
